#### 2a. Lo Type Definitions

**File: `D:\code\tutors-apps\cli\tutors-model-lib\src\types\learning-objects.ts`**

The core type hierarchy:

- **`Lo`** -- base type for all learning objects. Key fields: `type`, `id`, `title`, `summary`, `contentMd`, `contentHtml`, `route`, `img`, `video`, `hide`, `parentLo`, `parentTopic`, `parentCourse`, `breadCrumbs`, `frontMatter`, `authLevel`.

- **`LabStep`** -- a single step inside a lab: `{ title, shortTitle, contentMd, contentHtml, route, id, parentLo, type }`.

- **`Lab = Lo & { type: "lab", los: LabStep[], pdf, pdfFile }`** -- a lab is an Lo whose children are LabStep objects (not Lo objects).

- **`Talk = Lo & { type: "talk", pdf, pdfFile }`**

- **`Archive = Lo & { type: "archive", archiveFile? }`**

- **`Web = Lo & { type: "web" }`**, **`Github = Lo & { type: "github" }`**

- **`Note = Lo & { type: "note" }`**, **`PanelNote = Lo & { type: "panelnote" }`**, **`PanelTalk`**, **`PanelVideo`**

- **`Composite = Lo & { toc: Lo[], los: Lo[], panels: Panels, units: Units }`** -- container type

- **`Topic = Composite & { type: "topic" }`**, **`Unit = Composite`**, **`Side = Composite`**

- **`Course = Composite & { type: "course", courseId, courseUrl, topicIndex, loIndex, walls, wallMap, properties, ... }`**

#### 2b. type-utils.ts

**File: `D:\code\tutors-apps\cli\tutors-model-lib\src\types\type-utils.ts`**

```typescript
export const simpleTypes = [
  "note", "archive", "web", "github", "panelnote",
  "paneltalk", "panelvideo", "talk", "book", "lab",
];

export const loCompositeTypes = ["unit", "side", "topic", "course"];

export const loTypes: string[] = simpleTypes.concat(loCompositeTypes);

export const preOrder: Map<string, number> = new Map([
  ["course", 0], ["unit", 1], ["side", 2], ["topic", 3],
  ["talk", 4], ["book", 5], ["lab", 6], ["note", 7],
  ["web", 8], ["github", 9], ["archive", 10],
  ["panelnote", 11], ["paneltalk", 12], ["panelvideo", 13],
